# =====================================================================================
# empty.ttl — the empty-submission admission control (W2 · SP0, design §4: empty => REJECT).
# =====================================================================================
# A vacuous submission: it declares ZERO focus nodes for any algebra NodeShape (no
# rec:progenitor:record instance, no rung), so run-algebra-checks.sh step (b) treats it as an
# admission REJECT rather than a silent conforms=true pass (validation.log:34 idiom). This is the
# minimal control the runner requires (emp >= 1) so the T-PROG slice can run GREEN; T-FIX (Stage 2)
# owns the full fixtures/ tree. Deliberately triple-free (comments only) — an empty graph has no
# focus, which is exactly the vacuity the control asserts must NOT pass.
